CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ two-parallel-pack member alias: matched packs -> true: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ two-parallel-pack member alias: mismatched packs -> false: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
N5008 [temp.variadic]/4-5 + [temp.alias]/2.  A member alias template whose body
expands two parallel packs (its own pack + the enclosing class's pack) -- the
shape of libstdc++'s std::tuple _TupleConstraints
(__constructible/__convertible = __and_<is_X<_Types, _UTypes>...>::value, where
__and_ is a TYPE parameter pack) -- now expands in lock-step at the alias's point
of use.  Regression previously mis-expanded the alias's own pack during class
instantiation (fixed by "defer a member alias template's own-pack expansion
during class instantiation").  Non-vacuous: matched packs -> true, mismatched ->
false.  (An earlier version of this test used a recursive NON-type pack
`sum_t<...::v...>` proxy; that exercises separate non-type-pack defects tracked
by cpp11_nontype_pack_recursive_two_elem and
cpp11_nontype_pack_sizeof_expr_forwarded, not the tuple's type-pack shape.)
